caption: <$hgsd.pick>
title: $:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/docs/api/widgets/pick

! Introduction
A searchable popup picker for a single-value field: an edit-text handle that opens an 8-row listbox of candidates. Selecting writes the field and closes the popup; typing filters the candidates live (titles only, or titles + body + `gsd_project` in extended mode). The listbox is built as spec-valid HTML (option/optgroup children only).

The widget prescribes no display of its own (2026-09-01: no root wrapper — the handle input is a native inline element). It drops into any flow: inline inside a label, or as a flex item where the `hgsd-sizer-select` class (carried on the input) makes it stretch to fill the host row.

! Content and Attributes

|!Attribute |!Default |!Description |
|tiddler |— |Tiddler holding the field |
|field |`hgsd-pick` |Field to write (the temp field every pick consumer's Add/Save/keyboard/Create path reads — the suite-wide name; a call site may override it, e.g. the capture modal's `gsd_context`) |
|list-filter |— |''Required.'' Filter producing the candidate titles; drafts are always excluded (an inline `!is[draft]` on the funnel — they inherit the base tiddler's fields and would otherwise appear mid-edit) |
|placeholder |(blank) |Handle placeholder text |
|none-title |`-- none --` |Label for the empty choice |
|none-value |(blank) |Value written by the empty choice |
|group-by |(blank) |Field to group candidates into `<optgroup>`s (e.g. `gsd_project`) |
|none-group-title |(none) |Optgroup label for candidates without the grouping field |
|initial |(blank) |Handle's initial value when the field is empty |
|id |— |''Required for multi-instance correctness.'' Deterministic popup-state key; two pickers on one tiddler must differ |
|search-mode |`title` |`title` or `extended` (adds body text and `gsd_project` to the search) |
|focus |`no` |Focus the handle when the popup opens |
|realm-scope |`[subfilter<hgsd-realm-selection>]` |''An evaluated filter expression.'' See below |
|commit-kind |(blank) |Opt into instant commits — see below: `field` sets a single-value field, `append` appends the pick to a list field, `append-to-picked` appends `commit-value` to the ''picked'' tiddler's list field |
|commit-tiddler / commit-field |— |Commit target (tiddler title and field name) |
|commit-value |— |Value appended by `append-to-picked` |
|commit-clear |(blank) |State tiddler whose text is blanked on commit (collapses an edit-mode reveal) |

!! instant commits

With a `commit-kind`, selecting also commits the pick immediately — but only when the setting for the active pointer class is on: fine pointers (mouse) consult `$:/config/hypergsd/picker-instant-commit/fine` (default on), coarse pointers (touch) consult `$:/config/hypergsd/picker-instant-commit/coarse` (default off, keeping the Add step). With the applicable setting off, a pick only infills the field as before and the Add/Save button stays the commit step. The gates are evaluated at pick time, so toggling either setting or flipping the pointer takes effect on the very next pick; the pointer state itself comes from core's media-query tracking (`ui/config/pointer-coarse-tracker`). The buttons are never removed — they remain for an off setting and for typed non-existent titles (the create-and-add flow).

This tiddler also hosts `hgsd-pick-keyboard-commit`, the pick family's keyboard-commit dispatcher (2026-09-27; the key is the caller's `$keyboard` binding, Enter by default): invoked from the keyboard actions strings of [[$hgsd.pick-field|$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/docs/api/widgets/pick-field]] and [[$hgsd.pick-append|$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/docs/api/widgets/pick-append]], it reads the caller's ambient scope (`add-temp`/`target`/`field`/`direction`/`new-*`) and forks — a non-blank pick naming no existing tiddler (with `new-type` set) routes through the shared creation core `hgsd-create-and-add-actions`, everything else commits exactly as the row's own Add/Save button. The whole fork, existence check included, evaluates only at keypress.

!! realm-scope contract

The attribute is ''always'' evaluated as a filter; its output is the ''scope list'' — the allowed realm tags, plus the literal `no-realm` sentinel when realm-less items are included. The picker splits the list and applies the shared scoping arithmetic (`modules/realm-scopes.tid`).

| !Value | !Behaviour |
|omitted |the review sidebar's realm selection (`[subfilter<hgsd-realm-selection>]`); a missing state tiddler scopes to everything |
|`""` |''everything'' — falls back to `[subfilter<hgsd-realm-all>]` (every realm + realm-less; observably identical to no realm logic) |
|any other value |evaluated as given |

Because the value is just a filter, scopes compose:

```
<$hgsd.pick … realm-scope="[subfilter<hgsd-realm-all>]"/>                 <- every realm + realm-less
<$hgsd.pick … realm-scope="[[no-realm]]"/>                                <- realm-less items only
<$hgsd.pick … realm-scope="[subfilter<a>] [subfilter<b>] +[unique[]]"/>   <- composed
```

An unknown variable or broken filter yields an empty scope list — an empty picker (visible, self-explaining). Pristine sidebar state (no `$:/config/hypergsd/realm-selection` tiddler) scopes to everything, so the default filters nothing until a selection exists.

! Example
```
<$hgsd.pick tiddler=<<currentTiddler>> field="gsd_project" id="proj"
    list-filter="[tag[$:/GSD/Project]gsd_complete[false]sort[title]]"
    group-by="gsd_project" none-group-title="No group"/>
```